postedAt: 2026-07-26T23:20:00Z
title: "nox implements `builtins.parseFlakeRef` with one typed flake reference model"
tags: [nox, nix, evaluator, flakes]
links:
  - label: implementation
    href: https://github.com/indexable-inc/nox/pull/384
  - label: issue
    href: https://github.com/indexable-inc/nox/issues/368
---

`builtins.parseFlakeRef` now accepts a context-free flake reference string and returns its
exploded fetcher attributes. The evaluator rejects output fragments, relative bare paths,
non-string values, and strings carrying Nix store context.

One typed `reference::Attrs` model now owns flake references across parsing, registries, lock
computation, source resolution, the driver, and evaluation. The change removes the parallel
`reference::Input` enum and JSON lock attribute map. Source subdirectory selection is shared, and
`narHash` verification covers the full source root before `dir` selects a subtree.

A live differential matched Nix 2.34.7 on 652 of 652 JSON cases and 11 of 11 raw-byte cases. The
affected Rust suite passed 1,089 of 1,089 tests with 54 skipped.
